        },
        "consistency_check": "The most plausible value, 0.04, is inside [-0.28, 0.36]. A Student t distribution has unbounded signed support, including the possibility that saved clock is more valuable than the fatigue benefit; the interval is approximate."
      }
    },
    {
      "bucket": "intuition",
      "type": "offensive",
      "title": "Opponent-specific changeup package",
      "recommendation": "Install a small weekly package from an uncommon formation or motion family that contains two or three complementary plays, then use it early enough to force the defense to reveal its adjustment. Keep the package compact so the offense can execute it cleanly rather than adding a large menu of novelty plays.",
      "rationale": "The intended gain is to exploit opponent communication rules and create one or two high-value coverage errors before the defense adapts. Public EPA research does not cleanly isolate the value of surprise, opponent-specific formation preparation, and defensive communication stress, so this is an intuition-based recommendation rather than settled analytics.",
