      "type": "defensive",
      "title": "QB-specific scramble containment call",
      "recommendation": "Against quarterbacks who repeatedly convert third-and-medium with scrambles, call a limited third-down package that assigns one edge or second-level defender to preserve the quarterback's preferred escape lane instead of maximizing pure rush pursuit. Use it selectively when the down-and-distance makes a scramble conversion especially costly.",
      "rationale": "The tactic can prevent drive-extending scrambles but may reduce coverage flexibility or pass-rush pressure. Public analytics is mixed on spies and contain rules because assignment-level intent, quarterback escape tendencies, and coverage tradeoffs are not reliably observable in public data, making this primarily coaching intuition.",
