          "conversion_note": "student_t(nu, mu, sigma): nu = 4 and t_(0.975,4) approximately 2.78; mu = most_plausible_value = 0.08; sigma = (high - low) / (2 x 2.78) = (0.56 - (-0.40)) / 5.56 = 0.1727. Sigma is the t scale parameter."
        },
        "consistency_check": "The most plausible value, 0.08, is inside [-0.40, 0.56]. A Student t distribution has unbounded signed support, so it includes both a successful scramble-suppression effect and a harmful loss of pressure or coverage; the interval is approximate."
      }
    }
